xiv.org/abs/2602.24054","line":143},{"title":"pobox: External buffer processes to protect against mailbox overflow in Erlang","target":"https://github.com/ferd/pobox","line":144},{"title":"Blog post","target":"https://ferd.ca/handling-overload.html","line":145}],"metadata":{"title":"The Isolation Trap","source":"https://causality.blog/essays/the-isolation-trap/","author":["[[Causality]]"],"published":null,"created":"2026-03-14","description":"Erlang's mailbox design is more disciplined than Go's channels: only the owning process can read from a mailbox, and sends are asynchronous. Yet the four failure modes of shared mutable state still show up, just in different shapes.","tags":["#causality","#mpi","#mutability"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[38,48]]},"smart_blocks:resrc/clippings/The Isolation Trap.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"17lmivk","at":1778505719437},"key":"resrc/clippings/The Isolation Trap.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,13],"size":451,"outlinks":[{"title":"Causality","target":"Causality","line":5}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
