A paper","target":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.24054","line":52},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/73/Papers/027B.pdf","line":139},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://erlang.org/download/armstrong_thesis_2003.pdf","line":140},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://mariachris.github.io/Pubs/PADL-2010.pdf","line":141},{"title":"PDF","target":"https://mariachris.github.io/Pubs/TFP-2011.pdf","line":142},{"title":"arXiv","target":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.24054","line":143},{"title":"pobox: External buffer processes to protect against mailbox overflow in Erlang","target":"https://github.com/ferd/pobox","line":144},{"title":"Blog post","target":"https://ferd.ca/handling-overload.html","line":145}],"metadata":{"title":"The Isolation Trap","source":"https://causality.blog/essays/the-isolation-trap/","author":["[[Causality]]"],"published":null,"created":"2026-03-14","description":"Erlang's mailbox design is more disciplined than Go's channels: only the owning process can read from a mailbox, and sends are asynchronous. Yet the four failure modes of shared mutable state still show up, just in different shapes.","tags":["#causality","#mpi","#mutability"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[38,48]]},"smart_blocks:resrc/clippings/The Isolation Trap.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":"17lmivk","at":1778505810434},"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.08925748,-0.00854293,0.00032881,-0.01305398,-0.00969533,0.00133832,-0.00012885,0.01740977,0.00762377,0.03039825,0.03228911,-0.04543619,0.04022704,0.02290951,0.02199477,0.01149353,-0.06020454,0.02525669,0.03697489,0.05190371,0.07735661,-0.0379873,0.00965141,-0.07661086,0.04743254,0.08231322,-0.0175627,-0.04995526,-0.06461637,-0.25993556,-0.03445431,-0.01467003,-0.06068977,0.02601108,0.00632501,-0.04152047,-0.05653491,0.01373777,-0.00921211,0.00333638,-0.01636497,0.05526575,-0.04819157,-0.04253646,-0.04175778,-0.05788724,-0.01228421,-0.00803998,-0.00271169,-0.0617495,-0.055